E-PM2 (model E101): what the boot from the reset vector needs from om-emu's CPU, cores and interrupt controller.

For: om-emu, https://github.com/flatpanda/om-emu, commit 0819080133f6ca7edd455dfdfa209bd9eed291cc.
Apply after 0001-e101-function-harness.patch (tools/emu/setup.sh does both).

What it changes:
  emu/src/core/cores.mjs   an interrupt vector page per core (the E-PM2's CPU1 has its vectors in another page)
  emu/src/core/cpu.mjs     S.relax: a read of undefined flags gives the PSW's bits; a divide by 0 or an overflowing
  emu/src/core/interp.mjs  quotient gives a result with V set and counts in S.divz. Without S.relax nothing changes
  emu/src/dev/intc.mjs     board facts irq_kick, kick_cross (a bank's kick word raises the kick IRQ on the other
                           core) and lenient (unknown bank offsets are stored); a listener onMask(core, mask)
  emu/src/fw/models.mjs    the E101 entry's intc facts: irq_kick 124, kick_cross, lenient, ctl 0x3fc, and the parked
                           VSC and engine models on IRQ 50 and 54 (lines no E-PM2 device uses)
Used by: tools/emu/e101/*.mjs and tools/emu/boot/ (see tools/emu/boot/README.md).

Licence: the context lines are om-emu's (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 om-emu contributors; see
third_party/om-emu/LICENSE). The added lines are by the authors of epm2-tools, under the same MIT terms. See NOTICE.md.

